title: <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span> Party Vote
subtitle: Julius Curthose has resigned!
view-if: curtius_explosion_timer == time and gold_leader == "Curthose" and not lvp_formed
on-arrival: {!

if (Q.gold_relation < 35) Q.gold_right += 3;
if (Q.gold_relation >= 60) Q.gold_left += 3;
if (Q.in_grand_coalition) Q.gold_left += 2;
if (Q.liberal_parliament) Q.gold_left += 2;
Q.gold_right += 8;

if (Q.gold_right > (Q.gold_left*1.5) || (Q.gold_right > (Q.gold_left + 4))) {
    Q.gold_ideology = "Right"
} else if (Q.gold_left > (Q.gold_right*1.5) || (Q.gold_left > (Q.gold_right + 4))) {
    Q.gold_ideology = "Left"
} else {
    Q.gold_ideology = "Moderate"
}

if ((Q.pro_republic >= 80 && Q.gold_ideology == "Left") && Q.gold_reform && Q.traditionalist_leader != "Maine") Q.thiel_unlock = 1;
if ((Q.pro_republic < 80 || Q.gold_ideology != "Left") && Q.gold_reform && Q.traditionalist_leader != "Maine") Q.glatzel_unlock = 1;
if (Q.gold_ideology == "Right" && !Q.thiel_unlock && !Q.glatzel_unlock) Q.dingeldey_unlock = 1;
if ((Q.gold_ideology == "Moderate" || Q.gold_ideology == "Left") && !Q.thiel_unlock && !Q.glatzel_unlock) Q.kardorff_unlock = 1;

!}
max-visits: 1
tags: event
face-image: img/dvp.jpg
new-page: true

= <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span> Party Vote

Following the disastrous Freehold customs union project, of which he was the architect, he has tendered his resignation from both the Foreign Ministry and the leadership of the <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span>. This debacle has significantly discredited him and his allies on the party’s left wing, leading to a rightward shift within the <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span>, particularly at the local level.

An internal election must now be held to determine Curthose’s successor. With the industrial wing largely weakened, none of the leading candidates have particularly strong ties to Major Guilds. Caspar Holt and Florian Vellt, both members of the Clerks' Guild - a conservative white-collar Free Guild - and leaders of the <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span>'s Young Liberal wing, [? if not gold_reform: are the leading voices pushing for a genuine People's Party?][? if gold_reform: were instrumental in pushing the <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span> toward reform years ago?]. Meanwhile, Sigebert Strake, a veteran parliamentarian despite his past affiliation with the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span>, has significantly moderated over the years and was a close follower of Stratton, advocating for a Unity Coalition with the <span style="color: #c00000;">**Marchers**</span>. And, of course, Coalfax is running again, undeterred by his previous defeat.

- @thiel: Caspar Holt is elected!
- @glatzel: Florian Vellt is elected!
- @kardorff: Sigebert Strake is elected!
- @dingeldey: Soren Coalfax is elected.

@thiel
subtitle: Holt is a controversial unionist within the party, being more left wing than Vellt.
unavailable-subtitle: [? if not glatzel_unlock: The workers have no power within the <span style="color: #C0A054;">Golds</span>, and the wider party won't back a Free Guild member. ?][? if glatzel_unlock: Holt is still considered too left-wing for the party, and many prefer to back his colleague Vellt instead. ?]
choose-if: thiel_unlock
on-arrival: gold_leader = "Holt"; bourgeois_cooperation -= 3; gold_left += 10; coalition_dissent -= 1 if in_grand_coalition; gold_relation += 15; commons_gold += 6; commons_traditionalist -= 2; commons_other -= 2; commons_marcher -= 2; burgher_gold += 6; burgher_royalist -= 3; burgher_other -= 3; faithful_gold += 3; faithful_other -= 3; guild_gold -= 4; guild_traditionalist += 2; guild_kvp += 2 if kvp_formed; landed_gold -= 4; landed_traditionalist += 2; landed_traditionalist += 2 if traditionalist_ideology == "Moderate"; landed_kvp += 2 if kvp_formed; pro_republic += 5; ddp_left += 3; ddp_relation += 5
face-image: img/portraits/thiel.jpg

Surprisingly, Caspar Holt has been elected as the new leader of the <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span>! Compared to his colleague Vellt, Holt leans further left within the party’s unionist faction. He has even voiced support for increased welfare spending, arguing that austerity measures would only deepen the hardships faced by the people. In his push for national community, he has begun introducing more labor-friendly policies into the party’s platform, backing collective bargaining rights and worker protections.

As expected, the remaining guild-masters within the <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span> are outraged—even those with sympathies toward the late Stratton. This has led to a dramatic shift in the party’s financial backing, as funding from Major Guilds dwindles and is replaced by donations and dues from the Clerks' Guild and its affiliated members. [? if in_grand_coalition: We have noticed a significant decrease in coalition tensions. ?]

@glatzel
subtitle: Vellt, being a former member of the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span> as well, has shown nationalist sympathies.
unavailable-subtitle: [? if not thiel_unlock: The workers have no power within the <span style="color: #C0A054;">Golds</span>, and the wider party won't back a Free Guild member. ?][? if thiel_unlock: Vellt's views are too right-wing and nationalistic for the party, particularly given the current national mood. ?]
choose-if: glatzel_unlock
on-arrival: gold_leader = "Vellt"; bourgeois_cooperation += 1; gold_right += 3; gold_relation -= 5; commons_gold += 6; commons_traditionalist -= 2; commons_other -= 2; commons_royalist -= 2; burgher_gold += 6; burgher_royalist -= 4; burgher_other -= 2; faithful_gold += 4; faithful_other -= 2; faithful_traditionalist -= 2; guild_gold += 2; guild_traditionalist -= 2; landed_gold -= 4; landed_traditionalist += 2; landed_traditionalist += 2 if traditionalist_ideology == "Moderate"; landed_kvp += 2 if kvp_formed
face-image: img/portraits/glatzel.jpg
achievement: neuer_nationalismus

Florian Vellt is elected to become the new leader of the <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span>, being more nationalist and right-wing than his colleague Holt. He stands for a "New Nationalism," a solidarity among all classes, to defend the country's "living space" and to create freedom for the people. In his push for national community, to reduce the conflict between the classes, he has begun including more nationalistic and corporatist elements into the party platform.

As expected, the remaining guild-masters within the <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span> are worried, as the party begins to shift towards including the demands of the worker. This has led to a dramatic shift in the party’s financial backing, as funding from Major Guilds dwindles and is replaced by donations and dues from the Clerks' Guild and its affiliated members. His dynamic leadership should be closely watched.

@kardorff
subtitle: Strake is able to secure the continuation of Curthose's leadership.
unavailable-subtitle: [? if dingeldey_unlock: His closeness to Curthose has undermined his position. ?][? if thiel_unlock or glatzel_unlock: The party prefers a new and dynamic leader, preferably not one with closeness to Curthose. ?]
choose-if: kardorff_unlock
on-arrival: gold_leader = "Strake"; gold_left += 3 if in_grand_coalition; liberal_cooperation += 3; bourgeois_cooperation += 3; gold_relation += 5 if in_grand_coalition; burgher_gold += 4; faithful_gold += 2; landed_gold += 2; guild_gold += 2; pro_republic += 3
face-image: img/portraits/kardorff.jpg

Strake is elected to succeed Curthose as the leader of the <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span>. He is expected to be a continuation of Curthose's leadership, being another Stratton follower and supporter of constructive cooperation with the <span style="color: #c00000;">**Marchers**</span>. [? if ui0_seen: He even rallied his parliamentary faction to save our Unity Coalition back in 4294.?]

[? if bruning_time: He is also one of the strongest supporters of the Askew government, frequently coming into conflict with the right of the party over support for it. ?]

@dingeldey
subtitle: Coalfax aims to revert all of Curthose's progress.
unavailable-subtitle: The right-industrial faction of <span style='color: #C0A054;'>Golds</span> lacks the required influence.
choose-if: dingeldey_unlock
on-arrival: old_gold_leader = gold_leader; gold_leader = "Coalfax"; gold_right += 10; gold_relation -= 25; guild_gold -= 3; burgher_gold -= 6; landed_gold -= 4; pro_republic -= 5; ddp_cohesion -= 1; liberal_cooperation -= 5; bourgeois_cooperation -= 5
face-image: img/portraits/dingeldey.jpg

Soren Coalfax has unexpectedly won the vote to replace [+ old_gold_leader +] as chairman of the <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span>. Backed by broad and unified support from the party’s right wing, and endorsed by Reginald Eikenvorst, he has narrowly clinched victory against Strake.

Coalfax's election represents a significant and irreversible shift to the right,[? if gold_reform:&nbsp;with him even repealing Stratton's reform of the internal party structure,?] granting the guild-masters back their lost influence on the <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span>'s decision making. [? if chancellor == "Askew" and not marcher_in_government: Coalfax doesn't even feel great loyalty toward the Askew government and believes that the party could only fulfill its mission towards propertied concentration after it is freed from the burden of governmental responsibility.?] 

Furthermore, Coalfax is not particularly interested in a closer relationship with the <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span> and definitely not with us, but rather with parties to the right, such as the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span> and even the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Royalists**</span>, to transform them into a 'constructive component of the state.' This does not bode well for the future of Unity democracy.

